                                                "text": "[…] open your book of the play, which you have previously carefully perused, and at the same time marked with the proper calls, as thus: a length (or 42 lines) before an entrance, with a pen make a figure on the margin, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "647f2067-ba4c-4803-866e-77a81517c4f4",
                                                "sense_id": "f1187317-adcb-3819-9330-ae212b6fb456",
                                                "text": "The boy was engaged to write out parts at a penny a length (42 lines) for Chetwood, who then charged the manager, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b1297a6-8310-311f-85cc-a4ae4f64468b",
                                        "entry_id": "e83c3363-2007-360c-ac39-772b47705533",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The number of cards held in a particular suit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92d961dc-190b-4a10-becb-a78f5602f1e1",
                                                "sense_id": "0b1297a6-8310-311f-85cc-a4ae4f64468b",
                                                "text": "An artificial bid doesn't necessarily show length in the suit being bid, it has an altogether different meaning."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c993fe40-284b-3070-889c-8fd9e570d8b5",
                                        "entry_id": "e83c3363-2007-360c-ac39-772b47705533",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The amount of time for which the taste of wine lingers on the palate after swallowing or spitting it out, measured in caudilies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "length",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e5338f26-2d70-32cd-8707-18e1ed012f2a",
                                        "entry_id": "f4043b83-3ac5-3e9e-954d-918109cb621d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To lengthen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a7c5f4f-7ec1-4673-99c3-edced938c6bb",
                                                "sense_id": "e5338f26-2d70-32cd-8707-18e1ed012f2a",
                                                "text": "Pack night, peep day; good day, of night now borrow: / Short night, to-night, and length thyself to-morrow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f7be5f2-2eb8-4a2a-9e3c-770f287ecb72",
                                                "sense_id": "e5338f26-2d70-32cd-8707-18e1ed012f2a",
                                                "text": "Was never man such favour could off atall ladies fynde, To cause them lengthe or shorte the day which they to hym assynde."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8212570c-a04d-4a42-9e6d-3f7b4120b836",
                                                "sense_id": "e5338f26-2d70-32cd-8707-18e1ed012f2a",
                                                "text": "[He] knows full well life doth but length his pain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
